Sure! Here's a simple JavaScript function that switches the order of adjectives in a sentence:

```javascript
function switchAdjectives(sentence) {
  const words = sentence.split(' ');
  const adjectives = words.filter(word => word.match(/^(beautiful|green)$/));
  const reversedAdjectives = adjectives.reverse();

  const newSentence = words.map((word, index) => {
    if (adjectives.includes(word)) {
      return reversedAdjectives[index];
    } else {
      return word;
    }
  }).join(' ');

  return newSentence;
}

const inputSentence = "Beautiful green trees are in the park";
const outputSentence = switchAdjectives(inputSentence);
console.log(outputSentence); // Output: "Green beautiful trees are in the park"
```

This function splits the sentence into an array of words, filters out the adjectives, reverses their order, and then maps them back into the sentence at their original positions. The final result is the input sentence with the adjectives switched around.

