Here's a React hook that can be used to convert between different temperature units:

```javascript
import { useState } from 'react';

const useTemperatureConverter = () => {
  const [temperature, setTemperature] = useState(0);
  const [unit, setUnit] = useState('C'); // Default unit is Celsius

  const handleConvert = (toUnit) => {
    if (toUnit === 'F') {
      setTemperature((temperature * 1.8) + 32);
    } else if (toUnit === 'K') {
      setTemperature(temperature + 273.15);
    }
    setUnit(toUnit);
  };

  return { temperature, unit, handleConvert };
};

export default useTemperatureConverter;
```

To use this hook in your components, simply import it and call the `useTemperatureConverter` function:

```javascript
import { useTemperatureConverter } from './useTemperatureConverter';

const TemperatureConverter = () => {
  const { temperature, unit, handleConvert } = useTemperatureConverter();

  return (
    <div>
      <h2>Temperature Converter</h2>
      <p>Current temperature: {temperature} {unit}</p>
      <button onClick={() => handleConvert('F')}>Convert to Fahrenheit</button>
      <button onClick={() => handleConvert('K')}>Convert to Kelvin</button>
    </div>
  );
};

export default TemperatureConverter;
```

To edit the given text and give it a more professional tone, we can use a combination of HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Here's a step-by-step guide:

