Certainly! Here's an example of a PHP program that utilizes GROUP BY and HAVING clauses to refine the data and furnish a comprehensive roster of devoted customers:

```php
<?php
// Database connection details
$servername = "localhost";
$username = "username";
$password = "password";
$dbname = "database_name";

// Create connection
$conn = new mysqli($servername, $username, $password, $dbname);

// Check connection
if ($conn->connect_error) {
    die("Connection failed: " . $conn->connect_error);
}

// Query to retrieve customer information and purchase history
$sql = "SELECT c.name, c.email, p.product_name, COUNT(p.product_id) AS purchase_count
FROM customers c
JOIN purchases p ON c.customer_id = p.customer_id
WHERE p.product_name = 'specific product' AND p.date BETWEEN DATE_SUB(CURDATE(), INTERVAL 1 WEEK) AND CURDATE()
GROUP BY c.name, c.email, p.product_name
HAVING purchase_count >= 3";

// Execute query
$result = $conn->query($sql);

// Display results
if ($result->num_rows > 0) {
    // output data of each row
    while($row = $result->fetch_assoc()) {
        echo "Name: " . $row["name"]. " - Email: " . $row["email"]. " - Product Name: " . $row["product_name"]. " - Purchase Count: " . $row["purchase_count"]. "<br>";
    }
} else {
    echo "0 results";
}

// Close connection
$conn->close();
?>
```

This code will retrieve customer information and purchase history for customers who have bought a specific product at least thrice in a week from the transaction database. The GROUP BY clause groups the results by customer name, email, and product name, and the HAVING clause filters the results to only include customers who have made at least three purchases of the specified product within the last week.

